== 1.7 Chapter 1 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Matter is best defined as anything that],
  [occupies space and has mass],
  [can be seen],
  [has weight only],
  [can be compressed]
)

#mcq(2, [The state of matter with a fixed shape and a fixed volume is],
  [plasma],
  [gas],
  [solid],
  [liquid]
)

#mcq(3, [The change of a solid directly to a gas without passing through the liquid state is called],
  [condensation],
  [sublimation],
  [evaporation],
  [fusion]
)

#mcq(4, [Which of the following is a chemical change?],
  [boiling of water],
  [rusting of iron],
  [melting of ice],
  [dissolving sugar in water]
)

#mcq(5, [Which of the following is a physical change?],
  [grinding of pepper],
  [souring of milk],
  [digestion of food],
  [burning of paper]
)

#mcq(6, [An element is a substance that],
  [is always a metal],
  [cannot be split into simpler substances by chemical means],
  [contains two or more atoms],
  [has a variable composition]
)

#mcq(7, [A compound differs from a mixture because a compound],
  [has a variable composition],
  [can be separated by filtration],
  [has components in a fixed ratio by mass],
  [is always a liquid]
)

#mcq(8, [Which of the following is a mixture?],
  [sodium chloride],
  [water],
  [air],
  [carbon dioxide]
)

#mcq(9, [Filtration is used to separate],
  [an insoluble solid from a liquid],
  [two miscible liquids],
  [two dissolved solids],
  [a dissolved solid from its solution]
)

#mcq(10, [The liquid that passes through the filter paper in filtration is called the],
  [distillate],
  [supernatant],
  [filtrate],
  [residue]
)

#mcq(11, [The solid collected on the filter paper is called the],
  [filtrate],
  [distillate],
  [eluate],
  [residue]
)

#mcq(12, [A soluble solid can be recovered from its solution by],
  [using a separating funnel],
  [filtration],
  [decantation],
  [evaporation to dryness or crystallisation]
)

#mcq(13, [Which technique gives the purest crystals from a solution?],
  [evaporation to dryness],
  [crystallisation],
  [filtration],
  [decantation]
)

#mcq(14, [Simple distillation is most suitable for separating],
